[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 986,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 951,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149949,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 162,
        "headingId": 951,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Calcifying fibrous tumour is a benign lesion composed of a hypocellular fibroblastic proliferation with dense stromal collagen, chronic inflammation, and variably prominent psammomatous and/or dystrophic calcification.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 987,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 952,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149950,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 162,
        "headingId": 952,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>88170/0 Calcifying fibrous tumour</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 988,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 953,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149951,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 162,
        "headingId": 953,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>2E84.Y &amp; XA7MC7 &amp; XH7TH6 Calcifying fibrous tumour of stomach</p>\r\n<p>2E84.Y &amp; XA6452 &amp; XH7TH6 Calcifying fibrous tumour of small intestine</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 989,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 954,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149952,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 162,
        "headingId": 954,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> calcifying fibrous pseudotumour.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 990,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 955,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149953,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 162,
        "headingId": 955,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 991,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 956,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149954,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 162,
        "headingId": 956,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Calcifying fibrous tumour is anatomically ubiquitous with a predilection for the GI tract (especially stomach and small intestine), mesentery, and peritoneum {12232572;27196478;28153506;31355265}. Tumours usually arise in the submucosa or muscularis propria {20090503;28153506;30546412}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 992,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 957,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149955,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 162,
        "headingId": 957,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Patients are usually asymptomatic but may occasionally present with anaemia or abdominal discomfort {12232572;28153506}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 993,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 958,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149956,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 162,
        "headingId": 958,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Calcifying fibrous tumours may be detected over a wide age range, with a peak in young to middle-aged adults and no strong sex predilection described in published case reports {27196478;33066662}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 994,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 959,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149957,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 162,
        "headingId": 959,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 995,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 960,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149958,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 162,
        "headingId": 960,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Tumours are usually sporadic with rare familial cases {12817428}. The molecular pathogenesis is unknown.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1002,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 967,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149959,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 162,
        "headingId": 967,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>The tumours are well circumscribed and unencapsulated with a tan-white, firm, often gritty cut surface. The average size is 50&nbsp;mm (range: 5&ndash;250&nbsp;mm). Tumours are multifocal in around 5% of cases, mostly in the peritoneum {27196478}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 996,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 961,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149960,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 162,
        "headingId": 961,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Calcifying fibrous tumour is composed of a hypocellular proliferation of slender spindle cells with fine chromatin and indistinct cytoplasm, embedded in an abundant hyalinized collagenous stroma with a sparse lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate. Dystrophic and/or psammomatous calcification is observed in most cases. By immunohistochemistry, the lesional cells are usually positive for CD34 and rarely for SMA, whereas KIT (CD117), DOG1, desmin, STAT6, &beta;-catenin, and ALK are negative {11504838;12232572;31355265}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 997,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 962,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149961,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 162,
        "headingId": 962,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 998,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 963,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149962,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 162,
        "headingId": 963,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1001,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 966,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149963,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 162,
        "headingId": 966,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a circumscribed, hypocellular, densely collagenous mass with a sparse lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate, usually with dystrophic and/or psammomatous calcification.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 999,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 964,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149964,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 162,
        "headingId": 964,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1000,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 965,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 149965,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 162,
        "headingId": 965,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Around 10% of patients experience local recurrence {31355265}. There is no potential for metastasis.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:31:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]